[Submission_01.Objectives]
To hold the village of Lisov at any cost!
[Submission_01.Description]
At the end of 1944, the 501st Heavy Tank Battalion, after not very successful actions in the area of the Sandomierz bridgehead, received a new commander, Major Samish, instead of Major von Legat. The battalion was also renamed the 424th, due to the appearance of the 501st SS heavy tank battalion in the numbering system. In December 1944, the battalion was attached to the XXIV Tank Corps. On January 13, 1945, the battalion attacked the village of Lisov in Poland. The village was defended by the 61st Guards Tank Brigade, the 10th Guards Ural Volunteer Corps with several tanks of the 72nd Separate Guards Heavy Tank Regiment. As a result of a fierce battle, the 424th battalion was completely destroyed. Major Samish and the commander of the 61st Brigade, Colonel Morozov, were killed in battle.

[Submission_01.Success]
Victory
[Submission_01.Failed]
Defeat
